cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GaussCapture: local-first phone capture for 3D Gaussian splatting, with capture-time quality prediction"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Öz"
    given-names: "Enes"
    email: "enesozile@gmail.com"
    alias: "en970"
repository-code: "https://github.com/en970/gausscapture"
url: "https://en970.github.io/gausscapture/"
abstract: >-
  GaussCapture converts phone video into a 3D Gaussian Splatting preparation
  workflow that runs entirely on localhost, and is being extended into a
  research programme asking whether capture-time telemetry measurable on
  device predicts downstream reconstruction quality. The pipeline uses a
  fully permissively licensed component stack so that its outputs are
  unencumbered for commercial use.
keywords:
  - gaussian-splatting
  - 3d-reconstruction
  - novel-view-synthesis
  - capture-quality
  - photogrammetry
  - computer-vision
license: MIT
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-08-10"
